Chapter: RealCompareNegative

 Real ordering comparisons where BOTH operands are negative.

 `<`, `>`, `<=` and `>=` on Real were emitted as a SIGNED INTEGER compare of
 the two IEEE-754 bit patterns. That is right for two non-negatives and right
 for mixed signs, because a double's sign bit sits where the integer sign bit
 sits. For two negatives the order reverses, and every one of the four
 operators answered backwards.

 The four operators were the only numeric comparisons that ignored their
 operand type: `IrEq` and `IrNotEq` beside them already resolved it and sent
 Real to `ucomisd`, and the vector comparisons took it too.

 Two different code paths reach a comparison and each had the defect
 separately, so each case below is asked twice. A comparison in condition
 position is FUSED into the branch (`is-fusable-int-comparison`, and
 `lir-cmp-whitelisted` in the LIR); a comparison whose result is passed on as
 a value is MATERIALISED by `emit-binary-op`. Testing only one shape would
 have left the other broken and looked green.

 Every line prints the fused answer then the value answer, and both must be
 the number the line names.

Section: Operands

  neg-big : Real
  neg-big = 0.0 - 2.9

  neg-small : Real
  neg-small = 0.0 - 1.5

  pos-big : Real
  pos-big = 2.9

  pos-small : Real
  pos-small = 1.5

  zero : Real
  zero = 0.0

Section: The Two Paths

  b2i : Boolean -> Integer
  b2i (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  fused-lt : Real, Real -> Integer
  fused-lt (a) (b) = if a < b then 1 else 0

  fused-gt : Real, Real -> Integer
  fused-gt (a) (b) = if a > b then 1 else 0

  fused-le : Real, Real -> Integer
  fused-le (a) (b) = if a <= b then 1 else 0

  fused-ge : Real, Real -> Integer
  fused-ge (a) (b) = if a >= b then 1 else 0

  val-lt : Real, Real -> Integer
  val-lt (a) (b) = b2i (a < b)

  val-gt : Real, Real -> Integer
  val-gt (a) (b) = b2i (a > b)

  val-le : Real, Real -> Integer
  val-le (a) (b) = b2i (a <= b)

  val-ge : Real, Real -> Integer
  val-ge (a) (b) = b2i (a >= b)

Section: Report

  say-lt : Text, Real, Real -> Text
  say-lt (label) (a) (b) = label & " " & show (fused-lt a b) & show (val-lt a b)

  say-gt : Text, Real, Real -> Text
  say-gt (label) (a) (b) = label & " " & show (fused-gt a b) & show (val-gt a b)

  say-le : Text, Real, Real -> Text
  say-le (label) (a) (b) = label & " " & show (fused-le a b) & show (val-le a b)

  say-ge : Text, Real, Real -> Text
  say-ge (label) (a) (b) = label & " " & show (fused-ge a b) & show (val-ge a b)

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni (say-lt "neg-big lt neg-small want 11" neg-big neg-small)
    print-line-uni (say-gt "neg-big gt neg-small want 00" neg-big neg-small)
    print-line-uni (say-le "neg-big le neg-small want 11" neg-big neg-small)
    print-line-uni (say-ge "neg-big ge neg-small want 00" neg-big neg-small)
    print-line-uni (say-lt "neg-small lt neg-big want 00" neg-small neg-big)
    print-line-uni (say-gt "neg-small gt neg-big want 11" neg-small neg-big)
    print-line-uni (say-lt "neg-big lt neg-big want 00" neg-big neg-big)
    print-line-uni (say-le "neg-big le neg-big want 11" neg-big neg-big)
    print-line-uni (say-ge "neg-big ge neg-big want 11" neg-big neg-big)
    print-line-uni (say-lt "pos-small lt pos-big want 11" pos-small pos-big)
    print-line-uni (say-gt "pos-small gt pos-big want 00" pos-small pos-big)
    print-line-uni (say-lt "neg-big lt pos-small want 11" neg-big pos-small)
    print-line-uni (say-lt "pos-big lt neg-small want 00" pos-big neg-small)
    print-line-uni (say-lt "neg-small lt zero want 11" neg-small zero)
    print-line-uni (say-gt "neg-small gt zero want 00" neg-small zero)
  end
